<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Sulaym al-Aswani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Sulaym al-Aswani was a 10th-century Egyptian official and writer, sent around 969 by the Fatimid commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawhar-al-siqilli">Jawhar</a> as envoy to the Christian king of Makuria. His History of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>, now lost but quoted by later authors such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-maqrizi">al-Maqrizi</a>, is the main surviving description of medieval Nubia, including Makuria, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alodia">Alodia</a> and its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soba">Soba</a>.</p></div>
